<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>CSRF Labs - EliteHackLab</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/style.css">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/6.5.1/css/all.min.css">
</head>
<body>
  <div class="matrix-bg"></div>
  <nav class="main-nav"><div class="nav-brand"><span class="brand-icon">💀</span><span class="brand-text">Elite<span class="highlight">Hack</span>Lab</span></div><div class="nav-links"><a href="/"><i class="fas fa-home"></i> Dashboard</a></div></nav>
  <div class="lab-container">
    <div class="lab-header"><div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / CSRF</div><h1>🔄 CSRF Attack Labs</h1></div>
    <div class="lab-section">
      <h2><i class="fas fa-book"></i> Theory</h2>
      <p>Cross-Site Request Forgery tricks authenticated users into performing unwanted actions. If a user is logged in and visits a malicious page, that page can send requests to the vulnerable site using the user's session.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="lab-section">
      <h2><i class="fas fa-flask"></i> Labs</h2>
      <div class="lab-list">
        <% labs.forEach(function(lab) { %><a href="<%= lab.path %>" class="lab-link"><span class="lab-name"><i class="fas fa-terminal"></i> <%= lab.name %></span><span class="lab-difficulty <%= lab.difficulty.toLowerCase() %>"><%= lab.difficulty %></span></a><% }); %>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <script src="/js/main.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
